WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.280
X-ray scans of a 130-year-old museum rock uncovered a 100-million-year-old monocot flower with intact

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:12.640
three-part symmetry. It is the oldest direct record of that floral architecture. This is Planetarian

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:19.700
Daily, Episode 253. After the fossil, a leaf beetle enzyme that builds a medical toxin, common

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:25.080
pills that keep reshaping gut bacteria, and a Planetarian spotlight on plastics and dementia

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:31.100
brains. United States and United Kingdom researchers, according to Fizz.org, examined a rock

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:36.840
collected between the 1870s and the 1890s from the Dakota formation in Kansas and held

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:42.940
at the Smithsonian National Museum of Natural History. Micro-computed tomography or micro-CT,

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:48.800
scanning revealed a void left by a decomposed flower that measured 1.5 millimeters in height

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:56.720
and 1.2mm in diameter. The fossil shows three sepals, three petals, six stamens in two sets of three,

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.280
and three free carpals, a layout that most closely matches an extinct fan palm relative.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:09.140
Monocots make up roughly 20% of flowering plants and include cereals, bananas, yams, and orchids.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:15.280
Paleo-bottonist Professor Steven Manchester found the fossil by chance while scanning for another specimen

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:20.860
and botanist Walter Judd and paleobotanist Bruce Tiffney confirmed the monocot identity

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.560
during weekly online meetings.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:32.260
A cytochrome P450 enzyme named CCCYP9Z273 in the leaf beetle chrysalina sowirlens, reported

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:38.980
on BioRXIV, converts pregnant alone to carombellogenin through C14 hydroxylation.

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:47.480
Gene silencing of CCCYP9Z273 blocked cardinalide formation in the beetles, and isotope tracing

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:50.920
confirmed carombellogenin as an on-pathway intermediate.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:56.400
Mutagenesis at one active site residue switch the enzyme's product selectivity between

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.360
C14 hydroxylation and C15 hydroxylation.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.840
Cardinalides serve as chemical defenses in these beetles and are used medically as with

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:06.640
digitoxin.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:12.607
Most people assume that once a course of antidepressants, blood pressure medication or anxiety

00:02:12.607 --> 00:02:17.927
treatment ends, its influence on the body stops within days or weeks, but an analysis

00:02:17.927 --> 00:02:23.927
of more than 2,500 people, according to science daily, found those drugs still alter gut

00:02:23.927 --> 00:02:27.627
microbiome composition years after participants stopped taking them.

00:02:28.187 --> 00:02:32.947
Some anxiety medications produce shifts in microbial composition on the same scale as

00:02:32.947 --> 00:02:37.727
broad spectrum antibiotics, even though the drugs target the nervous system rather than

00:02:37.727 --> 00:02:38.287
bacteria.

00:02:38.947 --> 00:02:44.427
A few episodes back, wastewater bacteria from 8 Ohio cities serving 1.3 million people

00:02:44.427 --> 00:02:49.627
showed associations between gut patterns and local rates of obesity, high blood pressure,

00:02:49.927 --> 00:02:50.807
asthma and depression.

00:02:51.407 --> 00:02:55.887
This cohort adds the medications themselves as a lasting driver of those communities.

00:02:56.387 --> 00:03:01.367
The altered microbes sit inside the intestines that line the digestive tract and help regulate

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:06.747
nutrient absorption and immune signaling every day. Those persistent changes can affect how

00:03:06.747 --> 00:03:11.907
efficiently food is broken down and how inflammatory signals are generated long after the prescription

00:03:11.907 --> 00:03:17.607
bottle is empty. One practical step is to keep a dated list of past medications when discussing

00:03:17.607 --> 00:03:23.287
digestive or metabolic symptoms with a clinician, because the microbial record may still carry their

00:03:23.287 --> 00:03:28.827
imprint. Postmortem brain tissue from people with dementia, according to fierce biotech,

00:03:28.827 --> 00:03:33.967
Contained micro and nanoplastics at levels high enough to force re-examination of existing

00:03:33.967 --> 00:03:36.167
models of protein aggregation and clearance.

00:03:36.827 --> 00:03:42.067
The particles were absent or far lower in age-matched control brains without dementia diagnoses.

00:03:42.707 --> 00:03:47.227
Researchers note that the contamination may interfere with normal proteostasis pathways

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.207
long before clinical symptoms appear.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:55.880
Grim2AA, a DNA methylation clock, tracked in a large cohort followed for incident events,

00:03:55.880 --> 00:04:01.800
Raised the hazard of cardiovascular disease events by 6-11% for every one year increase

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:02.340
in the clock.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:07.080
The association was measured through incident events rather than cross-sectional data.

00:04:07.987 --> 00:04:13.207
A 194-year-old tortoise, according to Science Daily, carries sequence features linked

00:04:13.207 --> 00:04:15.607
to exceptional longevity and cellular maintenance.

00:04:16.227 --> 00:04:21.227
Genetic analysis of that animal uncovered those features, and the tortoise provides a natural

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:25.107
model for studying sustained cellular function across extreme life spans.

00:04:25.107 --> 00:04:31.421
A review of 40 studies found people with type 2 diabetes face a 53% higher risk of

00:04:31.421 --> 00:04:32.921
developing Alzheimer's disease.

00:04:33.461 --> 00:04:38.301
The same review calculated that nearly 5 of every 1,000 people with type 2 diabetes

00:04:38.301 --> 00:04:40.081
develop Alzheimer's each year.

00:04:41.054 --> 00:04:45.694
Clinicians identified a previously unrecognized inherited retinal condition that progressively

00:04:45.694 --> 00:04:50.154
damages peripheral and night vision while sparing central vision for years.

00:04:50.694 --> 00:04:54.094
Difficulty adjusting to darkness serves as an early clinical sign.

00:04:54.094 --> 00:05:00.583
A key structural feature of DNA turns potentially destructive ultraviolet damage into a form that

00:05:00.583 --> 00:05:02.223
cells can repair more easily.

00:05:02.863 --> 00:05:07.563
The mechanism may explain how early life survived intense solar radiation on Earth.

00:05:08.372 --> 00:05:13.532
Atmospheric organic nitrogen, quantified by a research team reporting through Fizz.org,

00:05:13.952 --> 00:05:17.092
supplies a significant nutrient source for marine ecosystems.

00:05:17.752 --> 00:05:22.472
The work established that contribution inside the global nitrogen cycle and integrates

00:05:22.472 --> 00:05:25.012
the input into global nitrogen cycle models.

00:05:25.911 --> 00:05:30.551
Hokkaido University researchers produced a previously unknown crystal structure of silver

00:05:30.551 --> 00:05:33.311
that exhibits unusually high chemical reactivity.

00:05:33.851 --> 00:05:37.031
The structure was observed only transiently before reverting.

00:05:37.771 --> 00:05:42.651
Chongqing's banan district teams, according to I Chongqing, have unveiled four class

00:05:42.651 --> 00:05:48.471
one innovative drugs for rabies, cancer, and leukemia, with three already marketed, two

00:05:48.471 --> 00:05:53.311
under review and 16 in development after they have antibody discovery timelines.

00:05:53.871 --> 00:05:58.651
Before we go, further longitudinal sampling of those medication-altered gut communities

00:05:58.651 --> 00:06:03.051
is what the microbiome analysis says will show whether they can be steered back toward

00:06:03.051 --> 00:06:04.131
a pre-treatment state.

